<title>RUSSIA: Russia names Bank of America its London Club agent.</title>
<headline>Russia names Bank of America its London Club agent.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian government named Bank of America its agent for the principal of its $35 billion debt to the London Club of commercial bank creditors, Deputy Finance Minister Mikhail Kasyanov said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Bank of America will register the $25 billion principal into five agreements in dollars, ecus, marks, Swiss francs and yen, and make payments to the creditors, Kasyanov said.</p>
<p>He said re-registering would start as soon as the London Club rescheduling is closed, which would be at the end of March or early April.</p>
<p>Russia would soon appoint an agent for securitising overdue interest and some interest payment into promissory notes (interest arrears notes), Kasyanov said.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
